  "description": "C8.6 neural canvas: learned clean two-state page reflow from x,y,t Learned warped/source coordinate features are included in the renderer MLP. Clean target fixture variant: deep-sea-lab. Decoder samples a cross latent neighborhood with 1px radius for local glyph/detail context in source mode. Decoder uses separate source and target-state branches, with the target branch sampling an independent target latent canvas and blending by midpoint progress (target hidden 160). Decoder also receives a separate state-split target-state latent canvas initialized at scale 0.02. Training directly samples 0.2 of points from the reflowed midpoint glyph/text distribution. A contrastive source-remnant loss (1) penalizes midpoint pixels that are closer to the source page than the clean target by margin 0.025.",
